.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-import 1  "dfdu-import " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-import \- Read a scan in ncdu\*(Aqs JSON format and print a summary (`dfdu \-f FILE` browses it)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu import\fR [\fB\-\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-top\fR] [\fB\-\-apparent\fR] [\fB\-\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-by\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read a scan in ncdu\*(Aqs JSON format and print a summary (`dfdu \-f FILE` browses it)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-depth\fR \fI<DEPTH>\fR [default: 1]
Levels of directories to print below the root
.TP
\fB\-\-top\fR \fI<TOP>\fR [default: 10]
Entries to print per directory, largest first
.TP
\fB\-\-apparent\fR
Show apparent sizes instead of disk usage
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fI<TYPES>\fR
Count only files of these types or extensions, comma\-separated: `video,audio,.iso`. Types: video, audio, image, document, archive, disk\-image, code, executable, font, data, other. Folders show the size of the matching files inside them
.TP
\fB\-\-by\-type\fR
After the tree, print disk usage by file type and the largest extensions
.TP
\fB\-\-bytes\fR
Print only the root total in bytes
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
The export (`\-` for stdin)
